<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Dec 7.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Dec 7.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended Dec 7</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE    % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				 (RS MLN)</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>State Bank	   210	   0.20     292900  61.51     4.97</p>
<p>Tata Steel	   153	   0.15     349950  53.54     5.11</p>
<p>Tata Power	   104	   0.12     167000  17.37     6.02</p>
<p>Gujarat Amb Cem    205	   0.03	48100   9.86     0.76</p>
<p>Arvind Mills	 112	   0.11	48650   5.45     5.12</p>
<p>Andhra Valley	 93	   0.12	51150   4.76     6.73</p>
<p>Tata Chem	    159	   0.16	27950   4.44     5.25</p>
<p>Bombay Dyeing	 97	   0.05	40100   3.89     2.69</p>
<p>G.E.Shipping	  28	   0.02     130900   3.67     3.72</p>
<p>Escorts		 76	   0.11	37800   2.87     7.55</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 4.85 percent on an annualised basis against 5.52 percent in the previous carry forward account ended Nov 30.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
